# Appointment lifecycle: book, replay, read, list, cancel, rebook (FR-6, FR-8, FR-9, FR-11).
# Run top to bottom with the VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client). Later requests reuse
# the id from step 1, so send them in order.
# Uses Hanoi at 15:00 tomorrow: Hanoi has one bay, so a cancellation visibly frees the slot.
# Meant to run once per day. On a second run, steps 1-2 replay the first booking and step 10 gets 409,
# because the first run's step 10 holds the slot. README › Try it explains how to reset.
# Needs a running API with seed data: `docker compose --profile app up --build` (see README › Try it).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
# "Tomorrow" in the dealerships' time zone (UTC+7, no daylight saving) = UTC date of now + 7 h + 1 day.
@day = {{$datetime 'YYYY-MM-DD' 31 h}}

@hanoi = 10000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003
@oilChange = 40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
@huy = 50000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005
@huyMazda = 60000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000007
@lan = 50000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004
@lanVios = 60000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006

### 1 · Huy books an oil change at Hanoi tomorrow 15:00 → 201 + Location header
# @name book
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/appointments
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: lifecycle-{{day}}

{
  "customerId": "{{huy}}",
  "vehicleId": "{{huyMazda}}",
  "dealershipId": "{{hanoi}}",
  "serviceTypeId": "{{oilChange}}",
  "start": "{{day}}T15:00:00+07:00"
}

### 2 · Same key, same booking → the same 201 and id, no second appointment (FR-11)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/appointments
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: lifecycle-{{day}}

{
  "customerId": "{{huy}}",
  "vehicleId": "{{huyMazda}}",
  "dealershipId": "{{hanoi}}",
  "serviceTypeId": "{{oilChange}}",
  "start": "{{day}}T15:00:00+07:00"
}

### 3 · Same key, different booking → 422 IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/appointments
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: lifecycle-{{day}}

{
  "customerId": "{{huy}}",
  "vehicleId": "{{huyMazda}}",
  "dealershipId": "{{hanoi}}",
  "serviceTypeId": "{{oilChange}}",
  "start": "{{day}}T15:30:00+07:00"
}

### 4 · Read it: customer, vehicle, bay, technician, times in UTC (FR-6)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/appointments/{{book.response.body.$.id}}

### 5 · Huy's appointments, newest first (FR-9)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/appointments?customerId={{huy}}

### 6 · Hanoi's appointments tomorrow (from inclusive, to exclusive; %2B is "+")
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/appointments?dealershipId={{hanoi}}&from={{day}}T00:00:00%2B07:00&to={{day}}T23:59:59%2B07:00

### 7 · Lan wants the same slot → 409 NO_SERVICE_BAY_AVAILABLE (Hanoi's only bay is Huy's)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/appointments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "{{lan}}",
  "vehicleId": "{{lanVios}}",
  "dealershipId": "{{hanoi}}",
  "serviceTypeId": "{{oilChange}}",
  "start": "{{day}}T15:00:00+07:00"
}

### 8 · Huy cancels → 200, status CANCELLED, cancelledAt set (FR-8)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/appointments/{{book.response.body.$.id}}/cancel

### 9 · Cancel again → 422 APPOINTMENT_NOT_CANCELLABLE (BR-12)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/appointments/{{book.response.body.$.id}}/cancel

### 10 · Lan tries again → 201: the cancelled appointment no longer holds the bay (BR-9)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/appointments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "{{lan}}",
  "vehicleId": "{{lanVios}}",
  "dealershipId": "{{hanoi}}",
  "serviceTypeId": "{{oilChange}}",
  "start": "{{day}}T15:00:00+07:00"
}

### 11 · Unknown id → 404 APPOINTMENT_NOT_FOUND
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/appointments/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000
